observed = "formerly observation.6.6.comet_genesis_boundary. GET /genesis is enabled only by LAYERX_PAXEER_COMET_URL, a literal loopback HTTP origin. It extracts the exact genesis JSON bytes from the configured Comet response and returns X-LayerX-Genesis-SHA256 over those bytes. The HTTP GET response shapes in paxeer-network/consensus/rpc/jsonrpc/server/http_server.go are bare results or errors; standard JSON-RPC envelopes are also parsed explicitly. Only the exact internal-error code, message and genesis_chunked data text permit ordered chunk retrieval. Counts, indices, base64 padding, JSON, chain_id, a separate 32 MiB genesis limit, 32-chunk cap and aggregate 30-second upstream timeout are checked. Existing EVM body bounds and method restrictions are unchanged. The primary boundary manifest configures http://127.0.0.1:26657. Tests execute the actual TLS binary against a loopback HTTP listener serving a byte-identical copy of paxeer-network/node/genesis/chains/pacific-1.json, including framing, exact-byte hashing, ordered reassembly, malformed input, size limits, timeout, unavailable upstream and unset-variable 404 cases. No new dependency or lockfile entry is introduced; serde_json raw_value preserves the returned representation and the existing rustls provider supplies SHA256."
assumption = "Full cargo test and platform-test-paxeer-boundary invoke tests/real_chain.py, which initializes and transacts on chain 125; the current isolation constraint prohibits those transactions. Focused genesis qualification does not establish the full real-chain gate or hosted deployment. The observer boundary must explicitly configure its own Comet origin http://127.0.0.1:26667, and identity evidence consumers must hash the exact response body before binding its chain_id to the EVM chain identity."
severity = "note"

