[observation.6.8.4]
task = "6.8"
file = "platform/hosted/tests/beta-cluster.sh platform/hosted/internal/deployment.yaml platform/hosted/webhooks/deployment.yaml platform/hosted/gateway/deployment.yaml platform/hosted/node/deployment.yaml"
symbol = "internal_principals_provision internal_apply manifests_render secrets_apply wait_ready"
observed = "formerly observation.6.8.internal-cluster-wiring. The image list and renderer include layerx-internal and its manifest. The generated beta CA issues Redis, KMS and four event-source certificates; runtime secrets bind KMS sealing and bearer material, Redis ACLs and event-source tokens. Payments and programs obtain separate read-scoped principal keys through the existing gateway POST /v1/keys route using the provisioned identity session. Human-backed journeys and approvals have TLS and service tokens but no invented principal credentials. The dashboard reads the existing gateway Redis with a read-only gateway:* ACL; the webhook Redis ACL permits its actual CAS Lua and webhooks:* keys. Source-grounded policies admit webhook component ingress at 9446 and payments/programs gateway ingress at 9443. The developer ConfigMaps expose each consumer's used dependencies. Internal workloads participate in readiness and internal namespace resources participate in teardown."
assumption = "bash -n platform/hosted/tests/beta-cluster.sh platform/hosted/tests/topology-check.sh exits 0 in qual-logs/au28/bash-n-final.log. ShellCheck is not installed, recorded in qual-logs/au28/shellcheck.log. bash platform/hosted/tests/beta-cluster.sh render exits 0 in qual-logs/au28/render.log. python3 qual-logs/au28/runtime-material-check.py exits 0 in qual-logs/au28/runtime-material-check-final.log after correcting the untracked harness's Lua literal extractor; the first harness invocation exited 1 in runtime-material-check.log before starting Redis. The final check validates six certificates against short/full Service DNS names, rendered internal image references, the real Redis production CAS Lua, gateway-data reads and cross-prefix/write/admin refusals. Both owned Redis processes use Unix sockets with no TCP listener and terminate. Image builds, gateway key issuance in Kubernetes and pod readiness remain unexecuted."
severity = "note"

[observation.6.8.5]
task = "6.8"
file = "platform/hosted/internal/deployment.yaml platform/hosted/tests/topology-check.sh platform/hosted/tests/beta-cluster.sh tools/qualification/beta_driver.py"
symbol = "LAYERX_EVENTS_UPSTREAM_URL LAYERX_EVENTS_CREDENTIALS_FILE qualification_url STACK_FLAGS"
observed = "formerly observation.6.8.human-upstream-blocks-expanded-topology. make platform-hosted-topology-check exits 2 in qual-logs/au28/topology.log. make platform-hosted-topology-check platform-beta-cluster-up platform-beta-cluster-down exits 2 in qual-logs/au28/task-6.8.log and task-6.8-final.log. Final output: topology-check: 43 edges, ok=40 external=1 note=10 failed=2. Verbatim refusal for both journeys and approvals: no Service layerx-testnet/layerx-human is declared in the manifests and it is not a declared separately operated service. Final make refusal: make: *** [platform/Makefile.inc:178: platform-hosted-topology-check] Error 1. The exact command stops before cluster creation or image builds. The unchanged journeys and approvals upstreams at internal/deployment.yaml:170,314 and credential-map paths at :172,316 require a real Human service and authenticated Human cookies; none is supplied by the hosted manifests. No hosted agentd Service exists either. The qualification exports leave Human and agentd unset without explicit overrides, and export the actual component boundary separately as LAYERX_AGENT_BOUNDARY_URL."
assumption = "CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=4 MAKEFLAGS=-j4 LAYERX_TEST_NATIVE_BIN_DIR=/root/lx-lanes/native-bin; LAYERX_BETA_KUBECONFIG unset; selected disposable kind identity layerx-au28-internal; LAYERX_BETA_MIN_FREE_GIB=30. qual-logs/au28/cluster-state.json records no selected cluster containers or built images. No image digest, pod readiness or live cluster teardown proof exists because the prerequisite failed. After confirming every render image reference was unbuilt and absent, supplementary make platform-beta-cluster-down exits 0 in qual-logs/au28/render-cleanup.log with LAYERX_BETA_KEEP_TOOLS=1; it removes render-only output, not a deployed cluster. remaining-cluster-containers.log is empty. df -h / is retained in disk-before-cluster.log, disk-after-exact.log and disk-after.log; free space remains above 30 GB. No persistent Paxeer endpoint, existing Redis endpoint or shared runtime is used. The missing-host assertion and separately operated status-publisher strict refusal remain intact."
severity = "blocker"

[observation.6.8.6]
task = "6.8"
file = "platform/hosted/tests/topology-check.sh platform/hosted/node/deployment.yaml"
symbol = "Topology.add check egress_admits load_builtin"
observed = "formerly observation.6.8.topology-model-and-existing-parser-limit. The checker now applies the supplied namespace only to documents without metadata.namespace, includes developer/internal manifests by default, follows ExternalName DNS chains without remapping the requested port, and checks DNS policy peers against kube-system/kube-dns labels. python3 qual-logs/au28/topology-regressions.py exits 1 in qual-logs/au28/topology-regressions-all.log: the current PyYAML model passes the 40 existing edges and retains the two missing Human failures; nine negative mutations detect alias cycles, missing/off-cluster alias targets, wrong target Service ports, selectors selecting no workload, invalid targetPort names, denied ingress, denied egress and denied DNS; explicit namespace precedence and the developer apply namespace pass. Full-parser parity remains failed: the built-in parser reports line 69 was not consumed for the node manifest. Running the unchanged HEAD checker and node manifest with bash qual-logs/au28/topology-baseline.sh --yaml-parser builtin qual-logs/au28/node-baseline.yaml also exits 1 with the same error in qual-logs/au28/builtin-baseline.log."
assumption = "The built-in parser defect precedes these changes and is recorded without altering its assertion or broadening the parser repair. This is static topology evidence, not pod connectivity or first-payment proof. cg spec lint exits 0 with zero errors and nine existing warnings in qual-logs/au28/spec-lint.log. git diff --check exits 0 in qual-logs/au28/diff-check.log. No spec task status changes or passing full-task gate are claimed."
severity = "blocker"

[observation.6.8.7]
task = "6.8"
file = "platform/hosted/tests/beta-cluster.sh platform/hosted/node/deployment.yaml platform/hosted/agent-boundary/src/main.rs platform/hosted/internal/src/events.rs platform/hosted/webhooks/src/trusted.rs"
symbol = "developer-component.token LAYERX_AGENT_BOUNDARY_GATEWAY_TOKEN_FILE LAYERX_AGENT_BOUNDARY_REGISTRY_TOKEN_FILE observe"
observed = "formerly observation.6.8.developer-component-token-and-observation-producer. The bring-up generates developer-component.token and mounts it for webhooks, while node/deployment.yaml:204-205 supplies only the distinct gateway and registry component credentials that agent-boundary/src/main.rs:428-429 loads and :1668,1676 authenticates. The webhook ReceiptVerifier calls that component in trusted.rs:459-488; admitting its network edge does not authorize its separate bearer. The internal event source requires authenticated POST /internal/v1/observe at events.rs:256 to capture a resource snapshot and bind it to its principal before serving an immutable event; bringing up its Deployment alone does not provide an observation/trigger producer."
assumption = "A dedicated webhook component credential contract and a real event observation/trigger integration need changes beyond the owned cluster-script and policy repair. No gateway or registry credential is reassigned to webhooks, no authentication check is weakened and no observation is fabricated. NEEDS.md contains the exact follow-up requests."
severity = "blocker"
