ir. Row 45 builds the qualification binary successfully and enters bounded-fuzz, then rustup attempts to provision the absent pinned nightly. The owned subprocess was terminated to honor the no-compiler-installation constraint. Verbatim final failure: Terminated; make[1]: *** [Makefile:2138: agent-fuzz-all] Error 143; make: *** [Makefile:2306: agent-qualify-fuzz] Error 1. Before termination the subprocess downloaded components and logged installation of cargo, clippy and rust-docs; full toolchain installation and fuzz execution are not established. qual-logs/r15/fuzz-toolchain-stop.log records the intervention; row-45.log retains the complete failure envelope. This is an interrupted prerequisite attempt, not a fuzz pass."
assumption = "The lockfiles pass locked offline resolution and their binaries build. Remaining compiler-prerequisite and Human test caller failures require their owners; no production or full wave qualification is claimed. No assertion or runner was changed."
severity = "blocker"

[observation.6.7.21]
task = "6.7"
file = "platform/hosted/human/deployment.yaml platform/hosted/human/Dockerfile platform/hosted/tests/beta-cluster.sh human/crates/layerx-human-service/src/server/production_components.rs human/crates/layerx-human-service/src/bin/layerx-human-components.rs human/apps/web/next.config.mjs"
symbol = "ProductionComponentsConfig ProductionComponents::open readiness session.open"
observed = "formerly observation.6.7.13 (renumbered after rebase). formerly observation.6.7.human-production-provider-hosting. The hosted Human image builds the real HTTPS API and privileged component binaries. The manifest exposes layerx-human on 9443 with beta CA TLS, an ephemeral shared component socket and persistent principal/custody/authentication-index storage. Every explicit LAYERX_HUMAN environment name is read by the service source. The API readiness route probes the production component graph and returns 503 when dependencies are unavailable. ProductionComponents additionally requires a real agentd Unix contract, framed security/identity/movement providers, mTLS custody KMS, Paxeer custody configuration, actor/authority/recovery inputs and authenticated storage keys. These are not furnished by the hosted HTTP identity and agent-boundary adapters or internal signing KMS. Mandatory layerx-human-components-config and layerx-human-component-material Secrets remain unprovisioned; no values are fabricated and no unspecified provider egress is granted."
assumption = "Ready Human hosting remains blocked on the provider graph and mandatory configuration. Source references and required integration requests are recorded in platform/hosted/human/README.md and the untracked NEEDS.md. Human session.open requires an indexed verified passkey assertion and real agent authority registration; journeys/approvals cookie maps remain empty. The Next.js standalone web application needs its own Node runtime and is not served as static files by the Rust API. The beta contract checker discovers hosted directories automatically; platform/docs/content/beta.md includes hosted-human without claiming runtime or deployment proof. No spec task status is changed."
severity = "blocker"

[observation.6.8.95]
task = "6.8"
file = "platform/hosted/tests/topology-check.sh platform/hosted/tests/topology-regressions.py platform/hosted/node/deployment.yaml"
symbol = "Chunk.parse_sequence Chunk.parse_block_scalar load_builtin"
observed = "formerly observation.6.8.topology-node-sequence-literal. The node manifest uses a YAML literal block as a sequence item in container args. The built-in parser previously treated the block indicator as an inline scalar and left its indented body unconsumed. Sequence block parsing now consumes that body and preserves the following env mapping. The regression compares the actual paxeer-relay args with PyYAML. make platform-hosted-topology-check exits 0 in qual-logs/au29/topology-final.log with both parsers: 43 edges, 42 admitted, one separately operated status-publisher edge and zero failures. Full topology parity, the original missing-Human baseline, all nine negative mutations and namespace precedence checks remain asserted. Adding the Human manifest removes exactly the two original missing-service failures."
assumption = "This is static topology and parser evidence, not runtime connectivity. The default make target now runs the built-in parser and persistent regression suite as well as PyYAML when PyYAML is installed. No assertion, bound, missing-host refusal or strict external-service refusal is removed."
severity = "note"

[observation.6.7.23]
task = "6.7"
file = "platform/hosted/human/Dockerfile human/Cargo.lock"
symbol = "layerx-human-service layerx-human-components"
observed = "formerly observation.6.7.human-image-lockfile-refusal. docker build --file platform/hosted/human/Dockerfile --tag layerx-au29-human:qualification --label io.layerx.au29=human - < qual-logs/au29/context.tar exits 1 before compilation because Docker interprets the uncompressed Python tar as an ambiguous Dockerfile source. Retrying the same tracked-source context compressed as qual-logs/au29/context.tar.gz reaches cargo build --locked --release --manifest-path human/Cargo.toml -p layerx-human-service --bins and exits 1, with Cargo exit 101: error: the lock file /src/human/Cargo.lock needs to be updated but --locked was passed to prevent this. Logs: qual-logs/au29/human-build.log and human-build-rerun.log. No Human image digest is produced."
assumption = "The Human workspace lockfile is outside the hosting paths. It is left unchanged and the Dockerfile retains --locked. bash -n platform/hosted/tests/beta-cluster.sh platform/hosted/tests/topology-check.sh exits 0 in qual-logs/au29/bash-n-final.log. bash platform/hosted/tests/beta-cluster.sh render exits 0 in render.log. python3 qual-logs/au29/check-human-manifest.py exits 0 in human-manifest.log, validating explicit env names against the service source, the readiness route, rendered images and beta CA verification for short/full Service DNS names and localhost. bash tools/ci/beta-contract-check.sh exits 0 in beta-contract.log. cg spec lint exits 0 with zero errors and nine existing warnings in spec-lint-final.log. timeout 60s cg review exits 124 in cg-review.log; cg guard exits 0 with advisory task-scope differences in cg-guard.log. These checks do not qualify a Human runtime."
severity = "blocker"

[observation.6.8.97]
task = "6.8"
file = "platform/hosted/tests/beta-cluster.sh platform/hosted/human/deployment.yaml"
symbol = "beta_cluster_up build_images wait_ready qualification_url"
observed = "formerly observation.6.8.human-cluster-disk-stop. make platform-hosted-topology-check platform-beta-cluster-up platform-beta-cluster-down passes topology with both parsers, builds layerx-testnet-control with image ID sha256:d95f0f8cbc5387a24afca7834f78d13463ee7ac587468faca36e59cb8b05e3b7, then is terminated with SIGTERM when free disk falls below 30 GiB during gateway image context loading. The process return code is -15, shell-equivalent 143. The canceled Docker build reports: ERROR: failed to build: failed to run Build function: Canceled: context canceled. Logs and results: qual-logs/au29/task-6.8.log, task-6.8-result.json, build-layerx-testnet-control.log, build-layerx-gateway.log, cluster-images.log and cluster-state.json."
assumption = "The selected disposable identity is layerx-au29-human with no owner kubeconfig or inherited LayerX overrides. CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=4 MAKEFLAGS=-j4, LAYERX_TEST_NATIVE_BIN_DIR=/root/lx-lanes/native-bin, LAYERX_BETA_MIN_FREE_GIB=30 and LAYERX_BETA_FORBIDDEN_CHAIN_ID=125 apply. No kind cluster or pods are created, no Human readiness probe executes and qualification exports are not written because env_write is not reached. The guard refuses contract transactions on the forbidden chain before deploy-contracts.sh; that step is not reached. The persistent Paxeer chain, existing Redis and shared runtime are untouched. Disk evidence is in qual-logs/au29/disk-before.log, disk-before-exact.log, disk-after-exact.log and disk-after-cleanup.log. Supplementary make platform-beta-cluster-down exits 0 in qual-logs/au29/teardown.log. remaining-cluster-containers.log and remaining-kind-containers.log are both empty; this proves cleanup and absence, not teardown of a deployed cluster. No complete cluster gate or ready Human deployment is claimed."
severity = "blocker"
