observed = "Version-2 evidence persists request_anchor, inclusion_checkpoint, network ID, native witness and signed recipient binding through client transport and Human stored plans. Native claim construction verifies committed account or withdrawal facts and recorded anchor ancestry; legacy evidence keeps its existing verifier. Version-2 vectors and deposit publication event digests are decoded with matching version enforcement. make test-native-withdrawal-proof regenerates a witness from real signed native asset dispatch and compares both Rust and Solidity copies. That gate, cargo fmt --check --manifest-path human/Cargo.toml -p layerx-paxeer-client -p layerx-human-service, cargo clippy --locked --manifest-path human/Cargo.toml -p layerx-paxeer-client -p layerx-human-service --all-targets -- -D warnings, cargo test --locked --manifest-path human/Cargo.toml -p layerx-paxeer-client, cargo test --locked --manifest-path human/Cargo.toml -p layerx-human-service --lib native_persistence_tests, and cargo test --locked --manifest-path human/Cargo.toml -p layerx-human-service --test exit --test withdraw all exit 0. Logs are qual-logs/set1/evidence-native-final.log, evidence-fmt-check-final.log, evidence-clippy-final.log, evidence-client-test-final.log, evidence-service-persistence-final.log and evidence-service-journeys.log. Local Foundry and Python virtual environment, repository paxd and build/bin native binaries were selected with 16 build jobs."
assumption = "These tests qualify native proof, wire, persistence and claim-construction source paths. Existing Anvil withdrawal and exit cases exercise legacy evidence, while deposit registration exercises version 2. They do not qualify native version-2 claim and fetch execution or autonomous producer publication."
severity = "note"

