[observation.6.8.113]
task = "6.8"
file = "platform/hosted/agent-boundary/src/main.rs platform/hosted/agent-boundary/tests/real_node.rs platform/hosted/node/deployment.yaml platform/hosted/webhooks/src/trusted.rs platform/hosted/webhooks/deployment.yaml platform/hosted/tests/beta-cluster.sh platform/hosted/tests/topology-check.sh"
symbol = "Plane::Webhook authenticate receipt_route component_secrets_generate read_secret_file"
observed = "formerly observation.6.8.4 (renumbered after rebase). formerly observation.6.8.webhook-component-credential. trusted.rs consumes GET /readyz and GET /internal/v1/receipts/{activity}, with a bearer loaded from LAYERX_WEBHOOKS_COMPONENT_TOKEN_FILE, trimming only trailing CR/LF and requiring 1..=4096 bytes. ComponentReceipt expects the unwrapped activity_id and receipt object. The gateway receipt tests encode a result wrapper; the registry internal receipt tests encode the raw object. Webhook admission uses the raw internal receipt contract, preserves registry access there, and refuses gateway submission/read routes and registry relay routes. There were no existing trusted.rs credential tests. The producer now generates independent gateway-component.token, registry-node.token and webhook-component.token through the existing write_token/OpenSSL path. Both namespace Secrets named layerx-webhooks-component-client use the same generated webhook file. The node reads its dedicated mount through LAYERX_AGENT_BOUNDARY_WEBHOOK_TOKEN_FILE; webhooks retains /run/layerx/tokens/component through a separate projected Secret. Configuration rejects a webhook token equal to either existing credential. The direct HTTPS Service endpoint and pod-port 9446 ingress/egress resolve in topology-check. Internal and developer manifests and bounded ExternalName resolution are included without treating missing Services or denied policies as passing. rustfmt and strict locked all-target clippy for layerx-platform-agent-boundary and layerx-platform-webhooks exit 0; logs qual-logs/au31/rustfmt-final.log and clippy-final.log. The initial clippy invocation exited 101 for start_boundary length; extracting the credential generation helper repairs that failure without suppressions. cargo test --locked --manifest-path platform/Cargo.toml -p layerx-platform-webhooks exits 0, three tests including the real generated-material consumer; qual-logs/au31/webhooks-tests.log. The combined locked crate test command exits 101, with four unit tests and seven real-node tests passing, including real_node_boundary_serves_the_component_contract and webhook_credential_configuration_refuses_shared_or_invalid_material. The former checks real generated webhook receipt bytes against the existing raw registry response and all gateway mutation scopes plus registry relay refusals; the latter runs the actual boundary binary against shared, missing, empty and oversized files. Initial dependency failures for Crypto and cryptography were resolved in qual-logs/au31/python; the final complete invocation remains failed in qual-logs/au31/tests-dependencies-ready.log. The two real escrow tests fail at tests/real_node/custody.rs:522 comparing protocol.batch_id() with receipt_execution_batch_id. Programs simulation and refusal-artifact tests fail at tests/real_node.rs:1828 and :2321 with 503 instead of 200, and Decode verification failures. These assertions and implementations remain intact. bash -n both scripts, beta-cluster.sh render, beta-contract-check.sh and git diff --check exit 0; logs shell-syntax-final.log, render-final.log, contract-final.log and diff-check-final.log under qual-logs/au31. cg spec lint exits 0 with zero errors and nine warnings; qual-logs/au31/spec-lint.log. make platform-hosted-topology-check exits 2; qual-logs/au31/topology-final.log. The webhook component edge passes both policies; other edges expose absent Human Service, gateway ingress refusals for internal payments/programs, pre-existing developer egress port mismatches and shared ConfigMap URLs inherited by dashboard. No topology assertion is skipped."
assumption = "Qualification uses CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=4 MAKEFLAGS=-j4 and LAYERX_TEST_NATIVE_BIN_DIR=/root/lx-lanes/native-bin, whose native-ready.txt identifies source c63b80eee91589422a9ecc6891c57b4dfa9a73aa. The real-node harness now honors that explicit binary directory. The final combined test also prepends qual-logs/au31/python/bin to PATH. Credential behavior is exercised on real TLS/native processes and actual generated material. Aggregate crate and topology gates remain blocked; no kind cluster, deployed Secret, pod readiness or production qualification is established. Remaining custody/Programs evidence and broader developer topology repairs require their owning tasks; task statuses are unchanged."
severity = "blocker"

