observed = "All literal base images used by the hosted Dockerfiles pull successfully, exit 0 in qual-logs/au41d/pull-bases.exit; the Paxeer wrapper uses the locally built paxd-node image. The exact command bash qual-logs/au39/run-gate-3.sh runs against revision 80ca83755471 and exits 2, recorded in qual-logs/au39/task-6.8.exit and qual-logs/au41d/wrapper.exit. Topology and refusal checks pass. All seventeen hosted images build and load, including dashboard-web and registry. Calico and both kind nodes become ready; the registry quota boundary service exits 0; disposable settlement bootstrap completes; the node reaches 6/6, registry 1/1 and all three gateways 1/1. Bring-up then fails because the Human port-forward does not accept TCP within its existing 60-second bound. Kubernetes reports FailedMount for volume component-material because Secret layerx-human-component-material does not exist. The Human Deployment requires that Secret, while beta-cluster.sh does not create it. Evidence: qual-logs/au39/task-6.8.log, qual-logs/au41d/human-events.log, port-forward-human.log, pods.log, boundary-status.log, images and build-*.log."
